For Question 2, the reasoning that matters most is the one that recognizes moral obligations extend through economic relationships to equals we may never meet. Option A captures this directly. But the equality framework doesn't license individual guilt as the whole answer — structural change matters (Option C), and the family's own legitimate interests as moral agents matter too (Option B), even if they don't outweigh the claims of the exploited workers.

