The son's equal moral status points most strongly toward respecting his own decision-making, with parental guidance playing a supporting rather than determining role. The reasoning behind this view is grounded in the principle that each person must form their own moral compass, while still acknowledging that we owe each other repair in community and that parents have real relational obligations.

