At the same time, recognizing that feelings of attachment are natural human responses — not malicious or chosen — is morally honest. The critique isn't that he is a bad person, but that he has failed in the specific duties his role demands. So for Question 1, options B and C both capture the core egalitarian verdict, with C adding nuance by acknowledging natural feeling. For Question 2, B most directly expresses the egalitarian principle that equal needs deserve equal treatment, while C explains how institutional roles enforce this obligation. Option A in both questions defends partiality in ways that conflict with equal standing.

